{"ratings":[{"id":"F1","consequence":"secret","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A failed run can publish private filesystem paths, and an unchecked fallback can also expose a configured private string."},{"id":"F2","consequence":"nuisance","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A transient posting failure followed by a status change can permanently omit a help notification after the run has already moved on."},{"id":"F3","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"unusual","reason":"A run active during the one-off upgrade can fail later without its issue receiving the failure label or comment."},{"id":"F4","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"unusual","reason":"A participant who copies a pending notification's marker can cause the factory to suppress its own notification permanently."},{"id":"F5","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A removed priority label can wrongly re-approve a failed issue, while a valid same-second approval can be refused."},{"id":"F6","consequence":"nuisance","trigger":"unusual","reason":"An unusually large history or notification backlog increases polling work and delays admission, without evidence of an outage or incorrect result."}]}